# Vendored third-party bundles are byte-for-byte what upstream shipped -- THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md's
# own rule for every one of them is "no local edits, ever, or the version stops describing what is
# shipped" -- and git's line-ending normalization is exactly that kind of edit: without this file,
# `core.autocrlf` rewrites every LF byte on checkout with no awareness of whether it sits inside a
# JS/CSS string literal or is merely source formatting. Found by the v3.2.0 release audit reviewing
# #504: `redoc.standalone.js` is 1837 lines, and several of its own minified string/template
# literals span more than one line, so an LF->CRLF rewrite on a Windows checkout could silently
# change what this app actually serves. The other vendored bundles
# (`htmx.min.js`, the two `swagger-ui-*.js` files) happen to carry at most one trailing newline
# today, so they are not reproduced instances of the same defect -- but the promise this file states
# is about every vendored bundle, not only the one that has already been hit, since the next
# version bump of any of them can introduce the same multi-line shape with nothing to notice.
# `-text` disables normalization outright, on checkin and checkout alike, which is what
# "byte-for-byte" actually requires -- git's own binary-file heuristic is not asked to guess, since
# it can guess wrong for a file that is technically text but must never be touched.
#
# **This rule is enforceable rather than aspirational since #510**, and that sentence is the one
# this comment used to have to make the other way round: for a release it read "nothing in this
# repository's CI verifies these bundles' served bytes against what was vendored, on any platform",
# which was true and left the rule resting on nothing. `THIRD-PARTY-DIGESTS.txt` now records a
# SHA-256 per vendored file and `tests/test_vendored_bundles_are_not_normalized.py` recomputes them
# on every leg, Windows included -- so a checkout that rewrote a byte inside a minified string
# literal fails the digest instead of silently serving different code.
src/requivo/web/static/vendor/** -text
src/requivo/api/static/vendor/** -text
